/******************************************************************************
* djinterp [restd]                                                     ranges
*
* ranges umbrella header:
*   Pulls in every public symbol of the <ranges> module that is
* currently shipped in restd. Mirrors the convention for #include
* <ranges> — users may include this header to obtain the full
* surface, or include the individual granular modules for finer
* control over compile-time cost.
*
*   STATUS:
*   - Phase R1:  foundations + primitive aliases + subrange + view_interface
*   - Phase R2:  range concept layer as SFINAE traits
*   - Phase R3:  view factories (empty_view, single_view, iota_view bounded)
*   - Phase R4:  range-wrapping adaptors (ref_view, owning_view, views::all)
*   - Phase R5:  take_view, drop_view, transform_view
*   - Phase R6:  filter_view, reverse_view
*   - Phase R7:  take_while_view, drop_while_view
*   - Phase R8:  join_view (lvalue-reference inner case, forward category)
*   - Phase R9:  unreachable_sentinel_t + unbounded iota_view
*   - Phase R10: range_adaptor_closure + operator| pipe syntax across
*                all shipped views::*
*   - Phase R11: as_rvalue_view (C++23) — pipe-enabled
*   - Phase R12: stride_view (C++23, forward category) — pipe-enabled
*   - Phase R13: chunk_view (C++23, forward category) — pipe-enabled
*   - Phase R14: chunk_by_view (C++23, forward category) — pipe-enabled
*   - Phase R15: slide_view (C++23, forward category) — pipe-enabled
*   - Phase R16: split_view (C++23, single-element delimiter) — pipe-enabled
*   - Phase R17: repeat_view (C++23, bounded + unbounded)
*   - Phase R18: join_with_view (C++23, single-value separator) — pipe-enabled
*   - Phase R19: as_const_view (C++23, simplified) — pipe-enabled
*   - Phase R21: output_range trait + viewable_range trait + lazy_split_view (C++20)
*   - Phase R22: internal utilities — restd::iter_move CPO +
*                iter_rvalue_reference_t (in iterator/), basic_const_iterator +
*                iter_const_reference_t (in iterator/), non_propagating_cache
*                + movable_box (ranges/internal/). Upgraded as_rvalue_view to
*                route operator* through iter_move, and rewrote as_const_view
*                as a thin wrapper over basic_const_iterator (dropping ~250
*                lines of duplicated iterator surface).
*   - Phase R23: range_rvalue_reference_t, range_const_reference_t,
*                constant_range — three one-liner traits over R22's machinery.
*   - Phase R24: ranges:: niebloid CPOs — begin / end / cbegin / cend /
*                rbegin / rend / crbegin / crend / size / ssize / empty /
*                data / cdata. All 13 in a single file using the same
*                priority<N> + poison-pill ADL pattern as iter_move (R22).
*                Live in restd::ranges:: sub-namespace to avoid collision
*                with the existing flat-namespace restd::begin et al.
*                ordinary-template overloads in <iterator>.
*   - Phase R25: join_view upgrade — removed the static_assert that
*                rejected prvalue inner ranges. The view now carries a
*                mutable non_propagating_cache; iterators use tag-
*                dispatched _materialize_inner / _current_inner helpers
*                so reference inners pay zero overhead while prvalue
*                inners route through the cache.
*   - Phase R26: repeat_view upgrade — stored value now lives in a
*                movable_box (the R22 utility). The view's default ctor
*                is well-formed for any T; non-default-constructible T
*                leaves the box empty until a value ctor populates it.
*   - Phase R27: movable_box sweep across the 5 callable-storing
*                adaptors — transform_view (m_fn), filter_view /
*                take_while_view / drop_while_view / chunk_by_view
*                (m_pred). Each adaptor's predicate or function is now
*                wrapped, giving the views proper view-concept-
*                compliant assignability even when the callable itself
*                is a non-assignable lambda.
*   - Phase R28: bidirectional upgrade — initially for stride_view,
*                chunk_view, slide_view; completed across chunk_by_view,
*                split_view, join_view, join_with_view. Each iterator's
*                category is now derived from the underlying via a
*                nested _bidi_clamp trait; bidi underlyings yield bidi
*                adaptor iterators. stride_view tracks m_missing to
*                recover the correct last stride boundary on -- from
*                end. join_with_view restructured ++ so canonical
*                separator state has m_outer at the next non-empty
*                inner (allows forward / backward equality).
*   - Phase R29: random-access optimisation for stride_view,
*                chunk_view, slide_view. _bidi_clamp lifted to allow
*                RA. O(1) operator+= / -= / +(n) / -(n) / [n] / it-it
*                plus ordering operators added to each. stride_view
*                uses the ideal-position (real + missing) calculation
*                for correct distance arithmetic across the m_missing
*                boundary; chunk_view + slide_view shift their cached
*                endpoints by n with clamping at m_base_end.
*
*   Deferred: common_view (blocked on common_iterator);
* range_common_reference_t (needs full common_reference chain);
* basic_istream_view (needs iostream); elements_view / keys_view /
* values_view, enumerate_view, zip_view, zip_transform_view, adjacent_view,
* adjacent_transform_view, cartesian_product_view (all need <tuple>);
* concat_view (needs variant); generator (needs coroutine); ranges::to
* (needs concepts + concrete container types).
*
*
* path:      /inc/djinterp/restd/ranges
* link(s):   TBA
* author(s): Samuel 'teer' Neal-Blim                       created: 2026.05.13
******************************************************************************/

